  "note": "calculateNIHSS(data) returns { nihssScore, nihssSeverity, firedRules } — no flags — so this is a SPLIT engine: the oracle pins detectAdditionalFlags(state) as expected.additionalFlags with flagsArgs [\"state\"], mirroring form-app.js's `detectAdditionalFlags(state)`. The 15 NIHSS items are summed with `?? 0`, so an unanswered item scores 0 and a blank form scores 0 = 'No stroke symptoms'; firedRules lists only items > 0 in catalogue order NIHSS-1A,1B,1C,2,3,4,5A,5B,6A,6B,7,8,9,10,11. Severity: 0 'No stroke symptoms', 1-4 'Minor stroke', 5-15 'Moderate stroke', 16-20 'Moderate to severe stroke', 21-42 'Severe stroke' — the label is always stroke-worded even for a non-stroke referral such as an epilepsy review (QUIRK). Flags verified: FLAG-STROKE-001 needs consciousness >= 2, any motor limb >= 3, or language >= 2; FLAG-STROKE-002 onsetType 'sudden'; FLAG-SEIZURE-001 statusEpilepticus 'yes'; FLAG-ICP-001 consciousness >= 2 AND redFlagWorstEver 'yes'; FLAG-ICP-002 mriCtFinding 'mass' or 'haemorrhage'; FLAG-IMAGING-001 mriCtFinding 'haemorrhage' — so a haemorrhage fires BOTH ICP-002 and IMAGING-001 (double-flag QUIRK); FLAG-HEADACHE-001/-002/-003 read the red-flag yes/no fields without checking headachePresent (QUIRK); HEADACHE-002 needs fever AND neck stiffness both 'yes'; FLAG-ANTICOAG-001 medium; FLAG-COGNITIVE-001 orientation 'disoriented'; FLAG-COGNITIVE-002 mmseScore < 24 (24 exactly does not fire); FLAG-MOBILITY-001 gait 'ataxic' or 'unable'; FLAG-EEG-001 eegFinding 'epileptiform'; FLAG-DISABILITY-001 mrsScore >= 4; FLAG-DRIVING-001 drivingStatus 'not-driving-medical' (low). Flags are stable-sorted high > medium > low; FLAG-ANTICOAG-001 is pushed before the headache flags but sorts after them. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas neurology-assessment --update",
